    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d216">

                <pb facs="0230" n="226" sameAs="frus:frus1938v03/pg226"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/13451: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-07-15T12:00:00-04:00">July 15, 1938—noon.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>443. Your 992, July 14, 6 p.m., proposed proclamation by the Shanghai Municipal
                    Council. Department’s 438, July 13, 4 p.m. outlines Department’s position in
                    regard to this matter.</p>
                <p>The Department perceives no objection to your acting in accordance with the last
                    sentence of paragraph 2 of your telegram under reference.<anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d216-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d216-f1" n="8" xml:id="d216-f1-content">
                <p>The proposed proclamation was promulgated July 18.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
